{{!
    @template local_elediaai_sources/activity_status

    Index status of one activity: badge plus a visible detail line (reason
    of a failure, next retry, "status not available"). Rendered inside the
    row's data-region="activitystatus" by the page and again by the status
    refresh, so both show the same words.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * status - Machine status: hidden, unknown, empty, indexed, queued, processing, error, unconfirmed.
    * statuslabel - Badge text.
    * statusclass - Badge classes.
    * statustitle - Optional title attribute (timestamp or raw message).
    * statusdetail - Optional visible detail line.
    * statusreason - Optional original message of the destination, shown below the detail.

    Example context (json):
    {
        "status": "error",
        "statuslabel": "Error",
        "statusclass": "badge-danger bg-danger",
        "statustitle": "PDF is encrypted",
        "statusdetail": "The file could not be read, for example an encrypted or damaged PDF.",
        "statusreason": "PDF is encrypted"
    }
}}
<span class="badge {{statusclass}} les-activity-badge" data-region="statusbadge" data-status="{{status}}"
    {{#statustitle}}title="{{statustitle}}"{{/statustitle}}>{{statuslabel}}</span>
{{#statusdetail}}
    <span class="les-activity-statusdetail small text-muted d-block" data-region="statusdetail">
        {{statusdetail}}
        {{#statusreason}}<span class="d-block">{{statusreason}}</span>{{/statusreason}}
    </span>
{{/statusdetail}}
